From: HD Satelit <dezvoltare@hdsatelit.com>
Subject: [PATCH] GLES: keep subtitle glyphs inside the Mali near clip plane

Mali-450 drops libass glyphs submitted at NDC depth -1 even with depth
culling disabled. Texture, vertex data, viewport and color mask are valid.
Keep the floor slightly inside the clip volume without moving any glyph
in X/Y or changing normal GUI depths. Only HiSilicon selects this patch.

Reproduced on u57 with external SRT and two embedded MKV subtitle tracks;
changing this shader alone makes all three visible over hardware video.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: HD Satelit <dezvoltare@hdsatelit.com>

diff --git a/system/shaders/GLES/2.0/gles_shader_simple.vert b/system/shaders/GLES/2.0/gles_shader_simple.vert
--- a/system/shaders/GLES/2.0/gles_shader_simple.vert
+++ b/system/shaders/GLES/2.0/gles_shader_simple.vert
@@ -25,3 +25,4 @@
   // set rendering depth
-  gl_Position.z = m_depth * gl_Position.w;
+  // Keep the glyph inside the near clip plane on legacy Mali drivers.
+  gl_Position.z = max(m_depth, -0.999) * gl_Position.w;
   m_colour    = m_attrcol;
